# DET-006 – New User Account Created

## Purpose
Detect the creation of new user accounts within the Active Directory environment.

## MITRE ATT&CK
T1136 – Create Account

## Data Source
- Windows Security Event Log
- Event ID 4720

## Detection Logic

```spl
index=windows host=DC01 "<EventID>4720</EventID>"
```

## Why This Detection Matters
Attackers frequently create new user accounts after compromising a system to maintain persistence or establish additional access. Detecting new account creation can identify unauthorized administrative activity.

## Expected Benign Activity
- Help desk creating new employee accounts
- Administrator provisioning service accounts
- Lab account creation
- User onboarding

## Potentially Suspicious Activity
- Accounts created outside normal business hours
- Unexpected administrator account creation
- Accounts created by unusual users
- Multiple account creations in a short period

## Validation

### Test Performed
Created a temporary Active Directory user account:

```
s8_testuser
```

Verified Event ID 4720 was ingested into Splunk.

Deleted the temporary account after validation.

## Investigation Notes
Review the following when this detection triggers:

- Who created the account?
- Which system generated the event?
- Was the account expected?
- Was the account immediately added to privileged groups?
- Was the activity approved through change management?

## Future Improvements
- Alert only on privileged account creation.
- Exclude known administrative service accounts.
- Correlate with group membership changes
